# `install.sh --pull` copies whole ~/.config directories back into the repo, so
# anything the live system keeps beside a managed config lands here too. These
# are per-machine state, not configuration -- they should stay out of commits.
Hyprland_Setup/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
Hyprland_Setup/gtk-4.0/thumbnail.png
# Superwhisper writes into three directories this repo deploys. Each file is its
# own, per machine: a backup of hypr/bindings.lua on every shortcut save, the
# WirePlumber drop-in its "keep microphone ready" setting adds and removes, and
# a PATH line its installer adds when ~/.local/bin was not on PATH.
Hyprland_Setup/hypr/bindings.superwhisper-*.bak
Hyprland_Setup/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/superwhisper-keep-inputs-ready.conf
Hyprland_Setup/fish/conf.d/superwhisper.fish

# Leftovers from the noctalia shell that GTK theming replaced. Deploying
# gtk.css drops the `@import url("noctalia.css")` that referenced them, but the
# orphaned files stay on disk until removed by hand -- and --pull would
# otherwise carry them back in.
Hyprland_Setup/gtk-3.0/noctalia.css
Hyprland_Setup/gtk-4.0/noctalia.css
